contentText:
Political satire, but make it jazzy. Randy Rainbow is once again using the power of song to tear into Donald Trump , this time reimagining Cole Porter &#8216;s classic &#8220;It&#8217;s De-Lovely&#8221; to say that he thinks the president is anything but.

The parody posted Tuesday (June 30) opens with the musical comedian portraying a news correspondent, editing clips of Trump from real interviews to make it look like the pair are having a conversation. After questioning the twice-impeached POTUS about his widely opposed handling of the Iran war, the setting shifts into a jazz club as Rainbow, wearing a retro tux, breaks into a song titled &#8220;He&#8217;s De-Mented.&#8221;

