&#8220;This dumbf&#8211;k tyrant seems to be the tyrant-ithesis of sanity,&#8221; he croons to the tune of Porter&#8217;s famous melody. &#8220;His screws are loose, his tangents roam/ The lights are on but no one&#8217;s home/He&#8217;s defective, he&#8217;s destructive, he&#8217;s demented.&#8221;

Rainbow &#8212; who&#8217;s made countless viral song parodies making fun of the president &#8212; goes on to change the original song&#8217;s lyrics to take aim at Trump&#8217;s old age and &#8220;decrepit&#8221; appearance. &#8220;It&#8217;s clear that Grandpa&#8217;s off his pills,&#8221; the Internet personality sings. &#8220;He can hear that bipartisan fear/ They&#8217;re united left and right: He&#8217;s in decline/ Time to resign.&#8221;

The video comes after the politician&#8217;s approval rating for the second-to-last week of June was calculated at just 34%, according to Reuters . Many of Trump&#8217;s past supporters in the conservative commentary landscape have turned against him , taking issue specifically with his approach to the conflict in Iran. Two months ago, Trump threatened that &#8220;a whole civilization will die tonight&#8221; if Iran failed to agree to a ceasefire deal; at press time, the U.S. is still in slowly progressing peace talks with Iran.

